  "full_text": "Well, so like I started, I've been kind of reckless, like almost starting a war. There's a story, King Wenceslaus, the peasant walked in his footsteps. I've been kind of reckless. And if somebody's, if I talked for a really long time and nothing was happening, I would get more and more reckless. Then all of a sudden I wake up and discover. Some teenagers are on board. Holy fuck. I've been reckless. So Dante's Inferno has the virtuous heathens in limbo, blowing around in limbo. That's kind of what I am, a little bit. Except it's not bad. It's not that bad. I'm like, some days I just feel like a pinball in a pinball machine. Just kind of bounce around. They think I'm going to get a job. No, I'm not going to get a job. It's the Truman Show. That's ridiculous. The whole thing is ridiculous. I'm in a pinball machine, and this is no time to be doing accounting or some shit. It's just freaking...",
